    {
      "block_id": "94d0561deb4e::b0004",
      "section_id": "94d0561deb4e::s002",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "heading_path": [
        "Buyer's Guide Engage - Early engagement",
        "Buyer's Guide"
      ],
      "markdown": "Early engagement By engaging with clients and offerors through early and ongoing consultation and dialogue, you are better situated to identify the complexities and risks associated with a client\u2019s requirement. It enables the development of mitigation strategies that places all stakeholders in a better position for a successful procurement that meets the client\u2019s needs. You, can also engage early with industry through various methods, such as issuing letters of Interest (LOI), Requests for Information (RFI), conducting one-on-one consultations and organizing industry days. Resources to support early engagement To ensure that you are successful initiating early engagement Public Services and Procurement Canada (PSPC) offers various resources. The resources available to you are: Acquisitions Program Policy Suite (accessible only on the Government of Canada network) which provides: policies, directives guidelines on engagement, communication, governance, socio-economic objectives risk management support Quick reference resources Procurement Information Nuggets (accessible only on the Government of Canada network) guides on procurement issues, offering quick references.",
      "plain_text": "Early engagement By engaging with clients and offerors through early and ongoing consultation and dialogue, you are better situated to identify the complexities and risks associated with a client\u2019s requirement. It enables the development of mitigation strategies that places all stakeholders in a better position for a successful procurement that meets the client\u2019s needs. You, can also engage early with industry through various methods, such as issuing letters of Interest (LOI), Requests for Information (RFI), conducting one-on-one consultations and organizing industry days. Resources to support early engagement To ensure that you are successful initiating early engagement Public Services and Procurement Canada (PSPC) offers various resources. The resources available to you are: Acquisitions Program Policy Suite (accessible only on the Government of Canada network) which provides: policies, directives guidelines on engagement, communication, governance, socio-economic objectives risk management support Quick reference resources Procurement Information Nuggets (accessible only on the Government of Canada network) guides on procurement issues, offering quick references."
    },
